WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:04.376
MacroLab: official macro data and econometric models, running in the browser.

2
00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:10.836
Start from the existing Same ECB shock template.

3
00:00:10.836 --> 00:00:19.361
Keep the existing method. Choose a common country window and conditional intervals.

4
00:00:19.361 --> 00:00:54.695
Run analysis. The calculation below is the actual browser run, without a time cut.

5
00:00:54.695 --> 00:01:00.824
Read Key facts and the Econometric specification before interpreting the response.

6
00:01:00.824 --> 00:01:07.441
Spain: cumulative real-GDP response to one identified ECB tightening shock.

7
00:01:07.441 --> 00:01:14.002
Germany: the same identified shock, on the same LP origin window.

8
00:01:14.002 --> 00:01:20.003
Shaded area: 68% pointwise conditional interval; it omits first-stage uncertainty.

9
00:01:20.003 --> 00:01:46.160
There is no cross-country equality test. Read the one-page case study for the limits.

